WEBVTT

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:18.520
It’s unbelievable...

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:23.500
Yet another Master Brain failed
to defeat Kaito Daimon.

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:25.960
What the heck is wrong with them?!

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:30.130
I’m sorry! I only have my
own shortcomings to blame...

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:34.820
Would you happen to have
any good game plans?

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:38.000
Didn’t you mention that Rook

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:41.020
has been sniffing around
Pythagoras’ Ruins lately?

00:00:41.380 --> 00:00:44.270
Yeah. What of it?

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:49.100
I just came up with something sweet.

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:54.920
By now, Kaito Daimon
and his pals should

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:57.160
have a good idea what this
journey’s really about.

00:00:57.610 --> 00:01:00.320
I can’t rely on Enigma anymore!

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:03.490
I’ll have to deal with them
with my own two hands...!

00:01:03.490 --> 00:01:06.670
You’ve made yet another
halfhearted puzzle.

00:01:07.370 --> 00:01:09.600
Do you truly believe you can

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:12.550
defeat Kaito Daimon off
of such a pathetic puzzle?

00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:17.670
Listen to me: Do whatever it
takes to realize your goal.

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:21.090
If you’re going to do
something, do it thoroughly.

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:23.100
Jin?

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:30.650
Isn’t it about time you
stopped and had some tea?

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:33.940
Y-yeah...

00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:37.030
That sounds good.

00:01:37.650 --> 00:01:39.320
Do it thoroughly...!

00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:16.000
She’s Too Shallow

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:30.010
Cough! Cough!

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:33.770
Sure enough, Herbert’s
information... led us to a trap!

00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:38.400
But we found out where
we’re supposed to go next!

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:40.070
I’m ready to go home!

00:03:40.070 --> 00:03:42.300
Iwashimizu wants to go home!

00:03:40.300 --> 00:03:43.650
All we’re gonna find is another
Master Brain waiting for us, right?

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:49.660
I, Ana, think we will have failed to
solve Rae-Rae’s puzzle if we quit!

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:55.650
Doesn’t it mean we’ve lost the
puzzle if we don’t obtain the prize, Jin?

00:03:55.650 --> 00:03:56.620
<i>It equals defeat.</i>

00:03:56.620 --> 00:03:57.920
Well, sure it does.

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:01.810
Let’s go! Let’s hit the next puzzle.

00:04:02.460 --> 00:04:06.430
That’s clearly Raetsel’s
trap. And you still wanna go?

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:09.890
I don’t care if it’s a trap or not.

00:04:10.330 --> 00:04:13.640
It’s the only way to find any clues
that will bring me closer to Jin.

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:15.910
Let’s go along with this game of hers.

00:04:16.390 --> 00:04:19.150
If she’s going to throw
a thousand puzzles at me,

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:22.320
then I’m going to solve
every single one of them!

00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:25.510
It looks like we don’t
have any other options.

00:04:25.510 --> 00:04:26.900
<i>We have no other choice.</i>

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:31.120
Just you wait, Raetsel!

00:04:31.990 --> 00:04:34.500
I swear that I will catch up to you!

00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:43.010
All right, Jin. I’m heading out now.

00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:45.460
Please hold down the fort, okay?

00:04:46.010 --> 00:04:46.890
Sure.

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:50.640
Please don’t go anywhere.
Promise me you won’t!

00:04:51.260 --> 00:04:52.640
I know.

00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:57.850
I’m sorry. I’m constantly
telling you what to do...

00:04:58.270 --> 00:05:02.330
It’s fine. I want to make you
and Kaito happy by recovering

00:05:02.330 --> 00:05:04.600
my memories as soon as possible.

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:08.530
I’m the one who should
be apologizing to you.

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:10.530
Jin...

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:14.290
I’m sorry I can’t
remember anything, Raetsel.

00:05:19.170 --> 00:05:21.970
I don’t care if your
memories don’t come back!

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:27.470
I’ll always be with you, even
if your memories never come back.

00:05:30.800 --> 00:05:34.350
Jin, I’m going to do a thorough job.

00:05:34.870 --> 00:05:36.350
I’ve decided to go through with it.

00:05:36.930 --> 00:05:37.980
So...

00:05:40.350 --> 00:05:43.730
...could you do one more thing for me?

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:53.700
This is the next puzzle, eh?

00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:55.460
All right! Let’s go!

00:05:55.460 --> 00:05:56.810
Stop!

00:05:58.540 --> 00:06:00.540
I’m against this after all.

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:04.550
There’s no point in continuing
these dangerous puzzles!

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:05.800
Nonoha, this is--

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:07.250
Even if everyone...!

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:11.400
Even if everyone is able to
continue solving puzzles,

00:06:12.220 --> 00:06:15.350
will this journey ever come to an end?

00:06:16.180 --> 00:06:17.500
Don’t you worry!

00:06:21.350 --> 00:06:23.560
Your journey will come to an end.

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:26.070
It ends right here--today!

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:27.820
Raetsel!

00:06:28.160 --> 00:06:31.820
Welcome! This will be your last stop.

00:06:31.950 --> 00:06:33.570
You’ve finally shown yourself!

00:06:33.570 --> 00:06:35.120
<i>You’ve shown yourself!</i>

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:37.580
What do you mean by “last stop”?

00:06:37.840 --> 00:06:41.310
I’m going to show you the
extent of my determination!

00:06:45.100 --> 00:06:46.040
Jin!

00:06:46.850 --> 00:06:50.810
Hey! It’s been a while,
hasn’t it, Kaito?

00:06:51.570 --> 00:06:53.400
Don’t be duped, Kaito!

00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:55.840
That could be the imposter, Jin Masaka.

00:06:55.840 --> 00:06:58.700
I, Ana, think that
Jin-Jin is for eal-ray.

00:06:58.990 --> 00:07:00.810
Jin, where are you?!

00:07:03.160 --> 00:07:04.980
Jin-Jin vanished...

00:07:05.540 --> 00:07:09.500
Jin is currently inside of this pyramid.

00:07:10.750 --> 00:07:15.220
If you can free my puzzle, the prize,
Jin, is yours for the taking.

00:07:16.050 --> 00:07:20.300
But if you fail, you’ll
never see Jin ever again.

00:07:22.430 --> 00:07:23.750
Let’s get started!

00:07:24.270 --> 00:07:27.710
This is a puzzle between you and
me that has Jin on the line!

00:07:43.370 --> 00:07:44.770
The rules are simple!

00:07:45.410 --> 00:07:50.040
Make your way through this maze and
reach the goal in the center alive!

00:07:50.210 --> 00:07:54.380
This maze...? But I don’t
see a maze anywhere!

00:08:05.640 --> 00:08:07.310
Now there are pathways!

00:08:07.310 --> 00:08:10.210
You want us to go for the goal when
we can’t see the overall picture?

00:08:11.770 --> 00:08:14.360
I’ve got electric currents flowing
across the top of the walls.

00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:17.180
So don’t think you can climb
to the top and study the maze.

00:08:17.900 --> 00:08:21.110
Do your very best as you try
to reach the prize, Jin!

00:08:22.030 --> 00:08:25.410
Brat! Have you completely
lost your mind?!

00:08:25.830 --> 00:08:27.020
He’s right!

00:08:27.020 --> 00:08:30.760
Don’t you care for Jin more
than anyone else in the world?!

00:08:30.760 --> 00:08:34.600
Jin told me that I’m
missing something!

00:08:34.920 --> 00:08:37.070
I’m sure that must
have been determination!

00:08:37.630 --> 00:08:39.200
Determination...?

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:41.580
And this is what you call
“determination”?

00:08:42.090 --> 00:08:45.080
I’ll do whatever it
takes to realize my goal!

00:08:45.390 --> 00:08:49.980
I’d be willing to sell my soul to the
devil if it’d help me defeat you!

00:08:50.770 --> 00:08:53.730
I swear that I will get Jin back.

00:08:54.610 --> 00:08:57.340
It’s puzzle time... Let’s start!

00:09:00.570 --> 00:09:03.990
The philosopher Pythagoras
had a puzzle here...?

00:09:06.410 --> 00:09:08.740
The prize has yet to be found,

00:09:08.910 --> 00:09:11.860
so people thought he abandoned
it before completion.

00:09:12.410 --> 00:09:15.210
But I recently learned that
this is where he put it.

00:09:16.130 --> 00:09:19.640
The truth behind the Puzzle
of God is said to be recorded

00:09:19.640 --> 00:09:21.620
in the Pythagoras Document.

00:09:22.050 --> 00:09:23.400
We’ve finally found it!

00:09:26.050 --> 00:09:29.020
I am terribly sorry, Master Rook.

00:09:29.020 --> 00:09:30.880
I will not be able to assist you.

00:09:31.520 --> 00:09:32.500
That’s fine.

00:09:33.140 --> 00:09:37.300
For now, let’s wait
for HIM to get here.

00:09:38.480 --> 00:09:41.640
I was being naïve. I was way too soft.

00:09:42.400 --> 00:09:46.450
Somewhere in my heart, a part of me
was showing mercy to Kaito Daimon.

00:09:46.780 --> 00:09:48.870
But I’m done hesitating!

00:09:50.040 --> 00:09:52.810
After this, my journey with
Jin will come to an end.

00:09:53.330 --> 00:09:55.200
The same goes for them...

00:09:57.170 --> 00:09:59.800
Q-taro, where’d Iwarin go?

00:09:59.800 --> 00:10:02.760
He said that he hates dank places.

00:10:02.760 --> 00:10:05.870
Kaito, this is our first
fork. Which way should we go?

00:10:06.340 --> 00:10:08.870
Let’s stick with the left-hand rule.

00:10:09.100 --> 00:10:14.230
Huh? Isn’t that when you head for
the goal while touching the wall?

00:10:14.640 --> 00:10:17.060
But aren’t there some mazes
where that doesn’t work?

00:10:17.060 --> 00:10:17.880
Really?

00:10:18.400 --> 00:10:19.540
Yeah, you’re right.

00:10:20.480 --> 00:10:24.190
When the starting point is on the
outside and the goal is in the center,

00:10:24.190 --> 00:10:26.900
there are instances when
hugging the wall won’t work.

00:10:28.280 --> 00:10:31.950
So we’ll keep that in mind
while hugging the wall...

00:10:35.290 --> 00:10:38.260
If we find a dead end, we’ll
skip that passageway.

00:10:45.510 --> 00:10:47.600
Follow your chopsticks hand next!

00:10:49.600 --> 00:10:52.400
Huh? Weren’t we following
the left-hand rule?

00:10:52.400 --> 00:10:53.670
No going left?

00:10:54.600 --> 00:10:56.460
Going left leads to a dead end.

00:10:56.690 --> 00:10:58.220
Huh? What makes you say that?

00:10:58.940 --> 00:11:01.720
Think back on the routes
we’ve taken thus far.

00:11:02.690 --> 00:11:06.650
You don’t need to go left to
know that it’s a dead end.

00:11:08.110 --> 00:11:09.480
I get it!

00:11:10.070 --> 00:11:15.500
The best way to solve this maze
is to play it by ear as you go.

00:11:22.170 --> 00:11:25.090
For such a grand prelude,
this is stinking easy!

00:11:25.090 --> 00:11:28.120
Yeah! This isn’t the least
bit challenging, is it?

00:11:28.970 --> 00:11:31.300
But something feels off.

00:11:31.760 --> 00:11:35.680
I can’t hear any voices
coming from this puzzle...

00:11:55.620 --> 00:11:57.520
Thank you for joining us,

00:11:57.660 --> 00:12:00.930
Mr. Pinochle and Mr. Freecell.

00:12:02.500 --> 00:12:04.780
I’m sorry to have asked
you to come out here.

00:12:05.000 --> 00:12:06.710
No, it’s fine.

00:12:07.420 --> 00:12:08.960
Let’s skip the formalities.

00:12:08.960 --> 00:12:11.160
Where is the philosopher
Pythagoras’ puzzle?

00:12:11.890 --> 00:12:13.010
This is it.

00:12:13.720 --> 00:12:15.170
It is...?

00:12:16.770 --> 00:12:19.400
The prize sealed inside is
the Pythagoras Document.

00:12:20.100 --> 00:12:21.900
It is believed that the
philosopher Pythagoras

00:12:21.900 --> 00:12:25.730
recorded the truth pertaining to
the Puzzle of God in this document.

00:12:27.030 --> 00:12:28.870
I am confident that it

00:12:28.870 --> 00:12:32.450
contains the hints we need to
help Jin recover his memories!

00:12:32.450 --> 00:12:34.700
We would like to request your assistance

00:12:34.700 --> 00:12:38.010
in order to obtain this prize, Mr. Freecell.

00:12:38.450 --> 00:12:41.070
But I wonder if I’m up to the task...

00:12:41.540 --> 00:12:42.830
I’m sure you are!

00:12:43.400 --> 00:12:47.070
You’re one of the Phi-Brain
children, so surely...!

00:12:47.860 --> 00:12:49.920
I’m not so sure about that.

00:12:50.260 --> 00:12:53.430
Freecell stopped solving
puzzles for a while.

00:12:53.680 --> 00:12:56.200
Being a Phi-Brain child
doesn’t compensate for that!

00:12:57.080 --> 00:12:59.090
Rook, can’t you handle
this on your own?

00:12:59.980 --> 00:13:02.980
His assistance is essential
if we are to free this puzzle.

00:13:03.690 --> 00:13:06.590
Two Phi-Brain children must
work together to release it.

00:13:07.110 --> 00:13:08.110
But...!

00:13:08.110 --> 00:13:09.650
Thank you, Pinochle.

00:13:11.110 --> 00:13:12.610
But I’m doing this.

00:13:13.320 --> 00:13:14.850
Freecell...

00:13:15.370 --> 00:13:19.700
I’ve been searching for something
that I could do to help Kaito.

00:13:23.670 --> 00:13:27.740
Let’s work together to
solve this puzzle, Freecell!

00:13:28.500 --> 00:13:30.240
Thank you, Rook.

00:13:39.970 --> 00:13:41.600
What’s wrong, Kaito?

00:13:41.810 --> 00:13:43.140
Something’s off.

00:13:43.140 --> 00:13:44.260
What is?

00:13:45.100 --> 00:13:46.840
Don’t you think it’s strange?

00:13:46.840 --> 00:13:49.140
This puzzle is way too shallow.

00:13:49.480 --> 00:13:51.940
Huh? It’s shallow?

00:13:49.480 --> 00:13:53.140
Yeah, for somethin’ meant
to crush us, she’s got the

00:13:53.140 --> 00:13:54.670
level cranked way too low!

00:14:03.620 --> 00:14:06.630
What the hell does Raetsel
have up her sleeve?

00:14:08.090 --> 00:14:10.660
Did she predict how we’d move...?

00:14:11.460 --> 00:14:15.130
Does that mean we’re doing
exactly what she expected?

00:14:16.840 --> 00:14:19.510
In that case, let’s check
out some of the other routes!

00:14:19.510 --> 00:14:21.680
Hey, Kaito! Where are you going?!

00:14:21.680 --> 00:14:23.630
That sounds good to me!

00:14:24.060 --> 00:14:25.170
Not you too, Gammon!

00:14:25.520 --> 00:14:27.270
Now what do we have here?!

00:14:46.750 --> 00:14:48.670
Are you okay, Kaito?

00:14:49.170 --> 00:14:50.210
Yeah...

00:14:50.210 --> 00:14:52.070
What’s taking you so long?

00:14:52.670 --> 00:14:55.580
Are you serious about
wanting to get Jin back?

00:14:56.930 --> 00:15:00.220
In the end, it looks like we’re
stuck takin’ the obvious route.

00:15:00.220 --> 00:15:02.510
I wonder if that’s really
the right thing to do...

00:15:02.890 --> 00:15:05.960
I, Ana, think Rae-Rae
is hiding something.

00:15:08.270 --> 00:15:09.220
I knew it!

00:15:10.150 --> 00:15:12.070
There aren’t any traps!

00:15:12.480 --> 00:15:18.030
I sincerely doubt Raetsel put her
heart into such an easy puzzle.

00:15:18.660 --> 00:15:22.090
Just maybe, Raetsel
wants us to solve it.

00:15:23.040 --> 00:15:25.960
Despite what she said about
her determination, deep down,

00:15:25.960 --> 00:15:28.240
maybe she wants to bring this to an end.

00:15:28.580 --> 00:15:32.130
Maybe she wants to give Jin back
and make up with you, Kaito.

00:15:32.340 --> 00:15:36.090
Do you think this puzzle is expressing
Raetsel’s inner feelings?

00:15:36.760 --> 00:15:40.180
Tch! Do you seriously
think she’s that sweet?

00:15:42.260 --> 00:15:43.400
I don’t know...

00:15:43.890 --> 00:15:47.240
I don’t know, but even assuming
that’s true, what gives?

00:15:48.100 --> 00:15:52.000
What’s with this ominous
feeling nagging at me?

00:16:01.730 --> 00:16:03.020
That’s the goal.

00:16:07.500 --> 00:16:09.900
In the end, we made it
here safe and sound.

00:16:10.790 --> 00:16:12.850
Is this really the puzzle she-

00:16:13.970 --> 00:16:16.530
-Raetsel made to show her determination?

00:16:23.350 --> 00:16:26.640
Now that I’ve come this
far, I have to keep going!

00:16:32.190 --> 00:16:34.480
Do you think Jin is in there?

00:16:43.570 --> 00:16:44.940
Hey! It wont budge!

00:16:45.410 --> 00:16:47.310
We freed the puzzle!

00:16:47.310 --> 00:16:49.570
Now keep your end of the
deal and give Jin back!

00:16:50.000 --> 00:16:52.500
Fine. I’ll return Jin.

00:16:53.130 --> 00:17:00.450
But, Kaito Daimon, are you prepared
to accept the truth about Jin?

00:17:02.800 --> 00:17:06.640
Upon regaining his memories,
he could start to hate puzzles.

00:17:07.010 --> 00:17:10.460
Could you welcome Jin with
a smile if he hated them?

00:17:11.060 --> 00:17:12.210
Let’s hear it!

00:17:13.400 --> 00:17:16.220
Well, she may have a point.

00:17:16.860 --> 00:17:17.970
Gammon?

00:17:18.440 --> 00:17:23.030
We seriously have no idea what lies
hidden within Jin’s memories.

00:17:23.660 --> 00:17:26.350
But we’ve had some nasty
shit thrown in our faces!

00:17:26.700 --> 00:17:29.370
The annihilation of all puzzlers...

00:17:29.370 --> 00:17:32.400
in accordance with a pledge
I swore to Jin Makata.

00:17:33.040 --> 00:17:35.670
I’ve come to learn that
it is highly likely that

00:17:35.670 --> 00:17:37.240
Jin Makata created these puzzles.

00:17:38.250 --> 00:17:41.790
I, Ana, think that the truth hurts...

00:17:42.550 --> 00:17:44.820
When Jin gets his memories back,

00:17:44.820 --> 00:17:48.290
what if he really does want
to annihilate all puzzlers?

00:17:48.810 --> 00:17:50.850
Just thinking about it
makes my skin crawl!

00:17:51.390 --> 00:17:54.050
That may be true, but...

00:17:54.400 --> 00:17:58.940
See! You have no right to receive Jin!

00:17:59.480 --> 00:18:03.180
It would be best for Jin
if he stayed with me.

00:18:03.490 --> 00:18:05.450
Yeah, you might be right.

00:18:06.160 --> 00:18:10.060
But it looks like Kaito
doesn’t feel that way!

00:18:10.740 --> 00:18:13.520
I won’t turn away from the truth!

00:18:13.530 --> 00:18:16.070
I’ll take any pain
that life throws at me!

00:18:16.460 --> 00:18:19.800
Yeah? So you wouldn’t care if Jin

00:18:19.800 --> 00:18:23.080
rejected you once he
regained his memories?

00:18:23.670 --> 00:18:26.080
You wouldn’t care if he abandoned you?

00:18:27.470 --> 00:18:29.460
Yeah, I wouldn’t care.

00:18:31.560 --> 00:18:35.710
Because I’d be sticking
to what Jin taught me!

00:18:42.190 --> 00:18:45.490
Do you ever think of them?
Of your mother and father?

00:18:47.870 --> 00:18:49.780
I could never forget them!

00:18:50.990 --> 00:18:52.910
And you don’t need to.

00:18:54.500 --> 00:18:58.040
Even if you look away,
it can’t undo the past.

00:18:59.630 --> 00:19:02.490
Don’t turn away from the truth.

00:19:03.290 --> 00:19:06.970
If you look away, you will never
be able to solve your puzzle...

00:19:08.050 --> 00:19:11.250
It’s the puzzle known as “life.”

00:19:19.190 --> 00:19:22.020
“Don’t turn away from the truth.”

00:19:23.360 --> 00:19:26.860
The one who taught that to
me was none other than Jin!

00:19:28.070 --> 00:19:31.530
Even if I look away, it
can’t undo the past!

00:19:33.410 --> 00:19:35.660
That’s why I solve puzzles!

00:19:35.660 --> 00:19:38.280
And I will grab hold of the truth!

00:19:40.460 --> 00:19:43.780
Now return Jin! Give Jin back to me!

00:19:45.010 --> 00:19:47.510
There really is no beating you.

00:19:47.510 --> 00:19:53.100
I’ll keep my promise.
You can have Jin.

00:20:00.860 --> 00:20:01.680
He’s in here!

00:20:01.980 --> 00:20:02.930
Jin!

00:20:07.820 --> 00:20:09.810
Aren’t you...? No way!

00:20:10.950 --> 00:20:12.450
You’re Jin Masaka!

00:20:14.120 --> 00:20:16.540
What the heck is an imposter
like you doing in here?!

00:20:16.540 --> 00:20:18.790
Where’s the Jin who
talked to us earlier?!

00:20:18.790 --> 00:20:23.320
I-I-I-I don’t know! She
just told me to stay in here!

00:20:29.470 --> 00:20:31.330
What’s this all about, Raetsel?!

00:20:33.050 --> 00:20:35.580
Just as promised, I’ve returned Jin.

00:20:36.220 --> 00:20:37.090
Why you...!

00:20:37.310 --> 00:20:40.440
I never said that it
would be Jin Makata.

00:20:40.940 --> 00:20:45.940
Did you honestly think I’d be that
quick to hand over the real Jin?

00:20:47.070 --> 00:20:49.700
You should know better than that.

00:20:51.070 --> 00:20:53.190
I’m going to transmit this to Kaito,

00:20:53.190 --> 00:20:55.070
but please don’t tell
him where you are.

00:20:55.070 --> 00:20:55.980
Why not?

00:20:57.100 --> 00:20:58.290
Please don’t...

00:20:59.710 --> 00:21:04.790
Nice try. Also, my puzzle
isn’t over yet.

00:21:06.460 --> 00:21:06.960
Wha--?!

00:21:06.960 --> 00:21:07.490
What?!

00:21:09.760 --> 00:21:11.050
The exit--!

00:21:12.640 --> 00:21:13.900
Didn’t I warn you?

00:21:13.900 --> 00:21:17.440
I’ll do whatever it
takes to realize my goal!

00:21:18.350 --> 00:21:21.140
Now then, it’s time for
the second stage to begin!

00:21:21.690 --> 00:21:24.900
However, you won’t be the Solver.

00:21:24.900 --> 00:21:25.630
Say what?!

00:21:30.650 --> 00:21:32.450
Please be careful, Freecell.

00:21:32.450 --> 00:21:34.660
Take care, Master Rook.

00:21:42.670 --> 00:21:44.650
Don’t you think it’s
about time you told me?

00:21:45.880 --> 00:21:46.780
Told you what?

00:21:47.340 --> 00:21:50.410
What exactly did he mean
when he said that it

00:21:50.410 --> 00:21:51.910
would take two Phi-Brain children?

00:21:52.550 --> 00:21:53.590
Well...

00:21:53.590 --> 00:21:56.350
Welcome to my puzzle!

00:21:59.520 --> 00:22:02.560
I don’t care diddly squat about
that philosopher Pythagoras.

00:22:02.560 --> 00:22:05.670
I’ve taken the liberty
to tweak this puzzle!

00:22:13.860 --> 00:22:20.120
Now then, let’s see the extent of
this kitten’s “determination.”

00:22:21.160 --> 00:22:22.320
Kaito?!

00:22:22.580 --> 00:22:29.090
Okay! With Kaito Daimon as your prize,
let’s begin our puzzle time!

00:24:01.970 --> 00:24:04.790
I shall rescue Kaito and the others.

00:24:05.100 --> 00:24:07.390
What is your plan of
action, Mr. Principal?

00:24:07.390 --> 00:24:10.400
I’m glad I set this up in the event
something like this should occur.

00:24:10.650 --> 00:24:11.980
Come in!

00:24:11.980 --> 00:24:15.650
Funga, Maze, Diceman,
Mr. Urban Development!

00:24:15.650 --> 00:24:18.740
POG Special Rescue Team, dispatch!

00:24:18.990 --> 00:24:22.030
Next time, “ If It
Were The Us of Then.”

00:24:19.580 --> 00:24:27.980
If It Were The Us of Then

00:24:22.030 --> 00:24:23.520
I just got a text from Kaito.

00:24:24.290 --> 00:24:27.200
It says they’ll pull through
on their own after all.

00:24:27.980 --> 00:24:30.990
Fin Art: Akeru Otsuki

00:24:27.980 --> 00:24:30.990
FORCED
